paint.setColor(Color.BLACK);
while(iterator.hasNext()){
    RectF rf = iterator.next();
    Rect r = new Rect((int)frame.left*(int)(1+rf.left),(int)frame.top*(int)(1+rf.top),(int)frame.right*(int)(1-rf.right),(int)frame.bottom*(int)(1-rf.bottom));
```

Implement a function `calculateIntersectionArea` that takes the main rectangle `mainRect` and a list of rectangles `rectList` as input and returns the total area of the intersection between the main rectangle and each rectangle in the list.

Function Signature: 
```java
public int calculateIntersectionArea(Rect mainRect, List<Pair<Point, Point>> rectList)
```

Example:
```java
Rect mainRect = new Rect(0, 0, 10, 10);
List<Pair<Point, Point>> rectList = new ArrayList<>();
rectList.add(new Pair<>(new Point(5, 5), new Point(15, 15)));
rectList.add(new Pair<>(new Point(8, 8), new Point(12, 12)));
int totalArea = calculateIntersectionArea(mainRect, rectList); // totalArea = 14
```

### Solution:
```java
public int calculateIntersectionArea(Rect mainRect, List<Pair<Point, Point>> rectList) {
    int totalArea = 0;
    for (Pair<Point, Point> rect : rectList) {
        int x1 = Math.max(mainRect.left, rect.first.x);
        int y1 = Math.max(mainRect.top, rect.first.y);
        int x2 = Math.min(mainRect.right, rect.second.x);
        int y2 = Math.min(mainRect.bottom, rect.second.y);

        int width = x2 - x1;
        int height = y2 - y1;

        if (width > 0 && height > 0) {
            totalArea += width * height;
        }
    }
    return totalArea;
}
```

