```
The function should extract `'emails/projects/members.created.message'` as the translatable string.

Write a function `extractTranslatableStrings($fileContent)` that takes the content of a Laravel language file as a string and returns an array of unique translatable string identifiers.

Function Signature: `function extractTranslatableStrings(string $fileContent): array`

Assume the following:
- The input file content will be a valid Laravel language file.
- The translatable strings will always be enclosed within the `__()` or `@lang` function calls.
- The translatable string identifiers will not contain any whitespace characters.

### Solution:
```php
function extractTranslatableStrings(string $fileContent): array {
    $translatableStrings = [];
    $pattern = "/__\(['\"](.*?)['\"]\)|@lang\(['\"](.*?)['\"]\)/";
    preg_match_all($pattern, $fileContent, $matches);

    foreach ($matches[1] as $match) {
        if (!empty($match)) {
            $translatableStrings[] = $match;
        }
    }
    foreach ($matches[2] as $match) {
        if (!empty($match)) {
            $translatableStrings[] = $match;
        }
    }

    return array_unique($translatableStrings);
}
```

The `extractTranslatableStrings` function uses regular expressions to match the translatable strings enclosed within the `__()` or `@lang` function calls in the input file content. It then returns an array of unique translatable string identifiers extracted from the file content.

