For example, given the input file containing the integers [1, -2, 3, 1], the cumulative sums would be [1, -1, 2, 3]. The first repeated sum is 1, so the function should return 1.

Function signature: `fn find_repeated_sum(file_path: &str) -> i32`

Assume that the input file contains one integer per line.

### Solution:
```rust
use std::collections::HashSet;
use std::fs;

fn find_repeated_sum(file_path: &str) -> i32 {
    let mut seen = HashSet::new();
    let mut cur = 0;

    let input = fs::read_to_string(file_path).expect("Unable to read file");
    let numbers: Vec<i32> = input
        .lines()
        .map(|line| line.parse().expect("Invalid integer in file"))
        .collect();

    seen.insert(cur);
    loop {
        for x in &numbers {
            cur += x;
            if seen.contains(&cur) {
                return cur;
            }
            seen.insert(cur);
        }
    }
}

